.\" Manual page for crankl.
.TH CRANKL 1 "2026-08-24" "crankl 0.5.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
crankl \- pack, inspect, compare, and run forward on compressed weight artifacts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crankl
.I COMMAND
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crankl
turns neural-network weight tensors (f32 files, .safetensors checkpoints,
GGUF models) into self-describing compressed
.I .crank
artifacts with provenance metadata, quality metrics, sheaf-cohomology health
gates, and inference support on the compressed form (Wilson-line holonomy).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI version
Print the engine version and AVX2 availability.
.TP
.BI pack " --input FILE [--output OUT.crank] [options]"
Pack a tensor into a .crank archive. Input may be a raw f32 file, a
.safetensors checkpoint, or GGUF. Options:
.RS
.IP "--tensor NAME"
pack one named tensor from a safetensors/GGUF checkpoint
.IP "--multi"
pack every F32 tensor of the checkpoint into ONE archive with an index footer
.IP "--pack-mode legacy|staged|bo"
select the pack objective (legacy is byte-identical to v1/v2)
.IP "--gguf"
write a GGUF container instead of .crank
.IP "--manifest FILE"
emit a format-version-2 JSON manifest (--multi)
.RE
.TP
.BI unpack " --input IN.crank [--output FILE]"
Reconstruct f32 weights from an archive.
.TP
.BI verify " IN.crank"
Validate checksums and structure; exits nonzero on any inconsistency.
.TP
.BI inspect " IN.crank [--json]"
Report metrics and sheaf cohomology (h0/h1). Multi-tensor archives also list
their tensor index. --json emits machine-readable output.
.TP
.BI compare " A.crank B.crank"
Similarity between two archives including the h1-weighted sheaf resonance.
.TP
.BI diff " A.crank B.crank"
Slot-level difference counts.
.TP
.BI turn " IN.crank [options]"
Anneal toward calibration targets (finetune on the compressed form).
.TP
.BI peel " IN.crank N"
Remove N history layers from an archive with a validated stack.
.TP
.BI holonomy " IN.crank [options]"
Run Wilson-line forward on compressed weights;
.B --batch N
applies N stacked input vectors through the batched AVX2 path (bitwise
identical to per-vector application).
.TP
.BI flow " SCRIPT"
Replay a pipeline script of the commands above.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success. Nonzero values are typed error codes (see
.IR include/crankl/errors.h );
corrupt or truncated inputs are rejected, never partially processed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I *.crank
Format v2 archive: header, slot payload, optional history stacks, META footer
with provenance and (for --multi) a per-tensor xxh64 index.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project docs:
.IR docs/API.md ,
.IR docs/CRANK_FORMAT.md ,
.IR docs/FLOW.md .
Technical report: docs/research/PAPER.md.
